{
  "summary": "P1 credential compromise (KB-029). Reported: Aisha Khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, not VIP, aisha.khan@brightline.example, device BL-LT-0105) clicked a link in a \"payroll verification\" email and typed her password into the page. Exact click time not given in ticket. Need to confirm with user. Checked: account active, sign-in not blocked, 0 failed logins, password last set 2026-09-09. Duo push enrolled on her phone. Sign-in logs (14 days, 9 events): all successful, all New York US, corporate or residential IPs (203.0.113.10 / 198.51.100.25), all Duo push, all within usual hours. No hosting-network, foreign, or MFA-denied events. Last sign-in 2026-10-08 13:35 UTC. So no attacker sign-in seen so far, and I did not request block_sign_in. Quarantine: Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of l), \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 08:23 UTC, marked phishing, not releasable. The copy she clicked may have reached her inbox, or other users may have received it. Worth checking for other recipients and purging. Done: password reset queued (approval #1). Verify her by callback to the number on file first, then give her the temporary password by phone. Still needed: approve the reset after callback; confirm the click time and whether she approved any Duo push or opened an attachment; keep watching sign-ins and block if anything suspicious shows up; check mailbox rules/forwarding for tampering; tell security about the lookalike domain and run a tenant-wide search for the message.",
  "reason": "KB-029 says always escalate; ticket is P1 credential compromise."
}
